/**
 * BlueprintBoard — the FLOW-FIRST blueprint surface (blueprint-v2), opened as an
 * EDITOR-AREA tab (wiring in renderer/blueprint/index.ts). A single legible
 * "drafting sheet": the full derived graph is rolled up (flow-model.ts) into
 * ~15 degree-ranked module cards in center columns, a left band of integrations,
 * a bottom band of datastores + the rolled-up CLI surface, inline dashed
 * proposal "ghosts", and aggregated curved wires between module centers.
 *
 * Design identity is SCOPED to this component (its own token layer — Prussian
 * paper in dark, vellum in light — via prefers-color-scheme defaults with
 * :root[data-theme] overrides in BOTH directions), so the board reads like an
 * engineering title sheet without leaking styles into the rest of the app.
 *
 * Data lifecycle (mirrors the retired BlueprintView, active-project scoped like
 * the git panel — ADR-002):
 *   first open → read + render (lazy — nothing fetched until opened); a missing
 *                graph auto-triggers blueprint:derive ONCE per root (never a
 *                user-facing command); a failed derive falls back to main's
 *                in-memory basic graph (blueprint:readBasic) so the tab never
 *                dead-ends. Pane logic reused from ./view-state.ts.
 *   setRoot     → follow the active project (rebind + refresh)
 *   handleChanged(rootId) → blueprint:changed re-read
 *   auto-derive pane / Recheck / failed-pane retry → re-derive under the hood
 *
 * DECORATION: decorate(anchors, flow) lights the cards a set of anchors
 * resolves to (ghosts pulse), dims the rest, and — only
 * when EVERY flow id currently resolves to a displayed card (whole-or-nothing)
 * — draws an animated dashed flow path with numbered hop dots. clearDecoration()
 * restores. Resolution rolls each id up to its displayed ancestor via
 * flow-model's buildDisplayResolver, so decoration lights the same card the
 * rollup drew. Motion is CSS, gated by prefers-reduced-motion.
 */
